<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deceneus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Deceneus was a Dacian high priest and adviser to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burebista">Burebista</a> in the 1st century BCE, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jordanes">Jordanes</a>. He is said to have helped Burebista unite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacians">Dacians</a> and to have persuaded them to cut down their vineyards and live soberly. Later sources present him as a teacher of philosophy and almost a co-ruler of the kingdom.</p></div>
